    <http://example.org/node/chunk1> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk10> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk11> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Call for tenders – City of Belval Implementation of an artificial intelligence solution of assistance to the agents City of Belval 1. Context and objectives of the project In the framework of City of Belval digital transformation strategy, City of Belval wishes to improve the efficiency of City of Belval administrative services and the quality of service rendered to the users. the agents are today confronted with a growing complexity of the procedures, with a multiplicity of the sources of information (regulations, internal procedures, business systems) and with an increase of the volume of requests to process. In this context, the local authority wishes to study and deploy an artificial intelligence solution allowing to assist the agents in the agents daily missions, notably to facilitate the access to the information, improve the quality of the answers and reduce the times of processing." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk12> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk13> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk14> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk15> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk16> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk17> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk18> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk19> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk2> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The present contract has for object the design, the implementation and the deployment of such a solution. 2. General description of the need The expected solution will have to allow to provide to the agents an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from the agents work environment, capable of accompanying the agents in the agents administrative activities. an intelligent assistance tool, accessible from their work environment, capable of accompanying them in their administrative activities could notably bear on: the search for information in the internal procedures and the applicable regulation, the help with the drafting of letters or of answers to the users, the accompaniment in the instruction of files (town planning, social aids, civil status, etc.), the suggestion of actions or of steps to realize in the framework of an administrative process. The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution into the existing practices of the agents and not constitute a rupture in the agents modes of work. 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk20> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "An accompaniment to the change and actions of training of the agents will be expected. 10. Criteria of evaluation of the offers the offers will be evaluated with regard to the following criteria: quality and relevance of the proposed solution, compliance to the regulatory requirements, level of security, global cost of the proposed solution, taking into account of the environmental issues, capacity of innovation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk21> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval is seeking a tender for an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents has a duration of 4 years, with a global budget of 3 million euros and an annual cost of exploitation that must remain compatible with The City of Belval budgetary capacities." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk22> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given our company's PM methodologies, past public sector references, consortium partners, available capacity, and governance practices as of 2024, what are the key factors our company's should focus on to ensure a coherent tender response?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk23> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure a coherent tender response for an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agentsject, our company's should focus on several key factors based on our company's context." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk24> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Firstly, given an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents duration and budget, our company's can leverage our company's experience in managing large-scale public sector projects, such as the Regione Lombardia AI-powered document management system project, which had a similar value and duration. our company's PRINCE2, Agile Scrum, and SAFe methodologies will enable our company's to effectively manage an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk25> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Secondly, considering the annual cost of exploitation constraint, our company's should emphasize our company's ability to provide cost-effective solutions while maintaining high service quality, as seen in our company's past references like the Comune di Torino digital workplace transformation project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk26> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Thirdly, since The City of Belval seeks an AI solution with a low environmental impact, our company's can propose integrating our company's solution with existing practices and systems, ensuring minimal disruption and optimizing costs. our company's partnership with GreenCompute S.r.l., specializing in Green IT and energy-efficient infrastructure, will be beneficial in addressing the environmental concerns." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk27> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Fourthly, to address the technical requirements and constraints such as integration with existing systems, data protection, and response times, our company's can highlight our company's technical expertise in AI solutions, ITIL v4 certification for service management, and experience with secure and efficient system integration." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk28> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Lastly, given our company's available project management capacity of 60% as of 2024 and our company's governance practices, including RAID logs, decision logs, change request processes, and steering committees, our company's are well-equipped to ensure transparent, controlled, and effective project delivery." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk29> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "By focusing on these factors and emphasizing our company's relevant experience, methodologies, partnerships, and capabilities, our company's can submit a strong and coherent tender response that addresses The City of Belval requirements and constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message3> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk3> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Functional scope The expected solution will have to cover the following functionalities: 3.1 Assistance with the consultation of information The expected solution will have to allow the agents to access quickly to reliable and up-to-date information coming from: the internal procedures, the applicable regulatory texts, the internal documents (guides, notes, repositories). The expected solution will have to be in measure to contextualize the answers in function of the demand of the agent. 3.2 Assistance with the drafting The expected solution will have to propose a help with the drafting of administrative contents, notably: answers to the users, administrative letters, syntheses of files. The generated contents will have to be adapted to the administrative context and compliant with the requirements of quality expected. 3.3 Assistance with the instruction of files The expected solution will have to be in measure to assist the agents in the analysis and the processing of files, by: proposing relevant information, recalling the applicable rules, suggesting actions or verifications to carry out." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk30> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution will have to integrate with existing systems of information, including business softwares (civil status, town planning) and electronic management of documents (EDM), provide times of response compatible with daily use by agents (< 2 seconds), guarantee a high level of availability (99.9%), and be hosted on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU. Can our current technical stack meet these requirements, and what architecture do our propose?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk31> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l., has experience with integrating existing systems of information through API integration, which is one of Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. primary domains of technical expertise. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can leverage Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. knowledge of API standards such as REST, GraphQL, and SOAP to integrate with business softwares like civil status and town planning, as well as electronic management of documents (EDM) systems like Alfresco or OpenKM." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk32> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet the response time requirement of less than 2 seconds, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can utilize Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expertise in Cloud architecture and containerisation using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) to ensure efficient resource allocation and scalability. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience with monitoring tools such as Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack will also help Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. maintain optimal system performance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk33> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding availability, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have achieved an availability of 99.92% on past projects, which is close to the required 99.9%. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can further improve achieved by implementing Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. security design patterns, including network segmentation, encryption, and secrets management using tools like HashiCorp Vault or CyberArk Conjur." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk34> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "As for hosting, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have experience with cloud providers that offer SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can deploy Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. solution on one of cloud providers that offer SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, such as Outscale (SecNumCloud) and OVHcloud to meet the hosting requirement." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk35> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of architecture, I propose a microservices-based approach, where each component is designed to handle specific tasks, such as API integration, document management, and user interface. a microservices-based approach, where each component is designed to handle specific tasks, such as API integration, document management, and user interface will allow Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. to scale individual components as needed and ensure high availability. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can also utilize Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. expertise in data engineering to design a robust data storage and retrieval system that meets the performance requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk36> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To provide intelligent assistance to agents, Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can leverage Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience with AI/ML systems, including large language models (LLMs) like Mistral 7B or LLaMA 3, which can be fine-tuned using methods like LoRA or QLoRA to adapt to the administrative context. Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can also utilize Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. knowledge of explainability tools like SHAP, LLaMA 3, and chain-of-thought prompting to provide transparent and trustworthy recommendations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk37> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, while there are some minor gaps between Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. current capabilities and the requirements, I believe that Our company, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. technical stack and expertise can be adapted to meet the client's needs with some additional design and implementation efforts." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message5> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk38> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution must comply with GDPR regulations, ensuring data is hosted exclusively in the EU, no data transfer outside the EU is authorized, and sensitive data is protected through encryption or anonymization if necessary." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk39> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, The solution should provide explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk4> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The expected solution will have to take into account the context of the file when this one is available. 3.4 Collaboration and continuity of processing The expected solution will have to facilitate the continuity of the processing of the files between agents and services, by allowing: a sharing of relevant information, an understanding of the context of an ongoing file, an effective resumption of the processing by another agent. 4. Regulatory and legal constraints The expected solution will have to imperatively respect the regulatory requirements in force. 4.1 Protection of data The holder will have to guarantee a strict compliance to the General Regulation on the Protection of Data (GDPR). To this title: the data will have to be hosted exclusively on the territory of the European Union, no transfer of data outside the European Union will be authorized, the data will have to be protected in an appropriate manner (encryption, anonymization if necessary). 4.2 Explicability and transparency the local authority expects that the recommendations or proposals issued by The expected solution can be explained." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk40> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What security controls and compliance measures do we need to implement to meet these requirements?" ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk41> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To comply with GDPR regulations and ensure the required security controls are in place, we will rely on we existing ISO 27001 certification, which covers the design, development, and operation of AI-powered information systems. we standard data residency is already set to the EU only, and we cross-border transfer policy prohibits data transfers outside the EU unless there's an explicit legal basis. we have anonymization tools in place, including Microsoft Presidio (self-hosted) and custom NER models, which can be used to protect sensitive data if necessary. we data subject rights implementation includes access, rectification, erasure, portability, and objection, ensuring we can handle data subject requests as required by GDPR." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk42> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To provide explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued, we AI security controls include output PII redaction, adversarial input detection, and confidence threshold escalation. our AI security controls will help ensure that we solution provides transparent and explainable outputs. we also have a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed, and a Data Protection Officer (DPO) contact information is available at dpo@nexus-engineering.it. we GDPR posture includes a data protection impact assessment (DPIA) capability, which we can use to assess the potential risks associated with we solution and implement necessary mitigations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk43> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In terms of technical security controls, we enforce multi-factor authentication (MFA) using TOTP and hardware tokens (FIDO2), and we have experience with role-based access control (RBAC) design. we network security architecture is based on zero-trust, micro-segmentation, and defense-in-depth patterns, and we have intrusion detection and prevention systems (IDS/IPS) deployed." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk44> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure the integrity of we logs, we use an append-only method with SHA-256 hash chaining, and we retain audit logs for 7 years. we also have a security incident response team (SIRT) in place, which can respond to security incidents and notify relevant parties within the required breach notification delay of 72 hours." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk45> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, by leveraging we existing security controls and compliance measures, we can ensure that we solution meets the required GDPR regulations and provides the necessary explicability and transparency of recommendations or proposals issued." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message7> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk46> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The tender requires strict GDPR compliance, explicability of AI recommendations, and no automated decision-making without explicit agent validation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk47> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The contract must also respect regulatory requirements in force." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk48> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What legal risks should we flag, and are we compliant with the necessary regulations, including GDPR and EU AI Act? we should flag typical legal risks such as open-source licence compliance, cross-border data flow, EU AI Act compliance evolution, and vendor lock-in mitigation." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk49> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, since all operations are intra-EU, cross-border data flow is not an issue.  we has expertise in EU AI Act, is aware of prohibited AI practices, and ensures human oversight and validation for automated decisions. we also have a no-automated-decision-without-human-validation policy, which aligns with The tender requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk5> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "It will have to be possible, a posteriori, to understand the elements having led to an answer or a suggestion. 4.3 Responsibility The expected solution will have to be designed as a tool of assistance. No decision will be able to be automated without explicit validation of an agent. 5. Technical constraints 5.1 Performance The expected solution will have to provide times of response compatible with a daily use by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk50> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Regarding GDPR compliance, we standard legal basis is Article 6(1)(e) – performance of task in public interest, and we have a Data Protection Agreement (DPA) template version 3.2. we are capable of performing data protection impact assessments (DPIA) and ensure that all client data remains we sole property." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk51> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Given the provided context, we appears to be compliant with the necessary regulations, including GDPR and EU AI Act, as we have measures in place to address these requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk52> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nevertheless, it is essential to continue monitoring updates to EU AI Act and other relevant regulations to ensure ongoing compliance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message9> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk53> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The total contract value is 3 million euros over 4 years, with an annual cost of exploitation that must remain within the local authority's budgetary capacities. The client expects cost optimization without sacrificing quality." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk54> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Are we financially eligible to bid, and what is the projected margin on this contract? Based on we company context, the maximum contract value we are eligible for is 3 million euros, which matches The total contract valuet. we average 3-year revenue is 3,950,000 euros, and we meet the minimum turnover threshold." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk55> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To determine the projected margin on this contract, let's consider we target gross margin percentage, which is 28%. However, since The client expects cost optimization without sacrificing quality, we might need to adjust we pricing strategy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk56> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The minimum acceptable margin percentage for we is 18%, but we typically aim for a higher margin. Assuming we can maintain we target gross margin of 28% on this contract, the projected margin would be approximately 840,000 euros (28% of 3 million euros)." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk57> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, this might not be achievable given The client emphasis on cost optimization. If we were to reduce our target gross margin percentage, which is 28% to the minimum acceptable level of 18%, the projected margin on this contract would be around 540,000 euros." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk58> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Keep in mind that these projections are based solely on our company context and do not take into account other factors that might influence the actual contract value or pricing strategy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message11> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk59> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our company context, the maximum contract value our are eligible for is 3 million euros, which matches the total contract value of this project. our average 3-year revenue is 3,950,000 euros, and our meet the minimum turnover threshold. To determine the projected margin, letour consider our target gross margin percentage, which is 28%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk6> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To indicative title, a time of response lower than 2 seconds is expected for the current requests. A high level of relevance of the answers is expected. 5.2 Availability The expected solution will have to guarantee a high level of availability, compatible with the needs of the municipal services. An objective of availability of the order of 99.9% is expected. 5.3 Integration The expected solution will have to integrate The expected solution with the existing system of information, notably: the business softwares (civil status, town planning), the electronic management of documents (EDM), the user directories." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk60> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, since the client expects cost optimization without sacrificing quality, our might need to adjust our pricing strategy. The minimum acceptable margin percentage for our is 18%, but our typically aim for a higher margin." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk61> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Assuming our can maintain our target gross margin percentage, which is 28% on this project, the projected margin would be approximately 840,000 euros (28% of 3 million euros). However, this might not be achievable given the client emphasis on cost optimization." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk62> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "If our were to reduce the projected margin to the minimum acceptable level of 18%, the projected margin would be around 540,000 euros. Keep in mind that these projections are based solely on our company context and do not take into account other factors that might influence the actual contract value or pricing strategy." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk63> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Based on our company context, the maximum contract value we are eligible forr is 3 million euros, as specified in the tender eligibility section of our context data. the maximum contract value we are eligible for matches the total contract value of this project. As for the projected margin, our context data provides a target gross margin percentage of 28% and a minimum acceptable margin percentage of 18%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk64> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, our context data does not contain any information that would allow our to calculate a specific projected margin for this project. Therefore, I do not have enough information to provide a projected margin on this project." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message12> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk65> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The solution should provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents, facilitating access to information, improving answer quality, and reducing processing times. The solution must also integrate with existing systems and provide explicability of recommendations." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk66> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What AI components and innovation strategy do we propose to meet these requirements, and what are the known trade-offs? Based on we company context, we propose a solution that leverages we expertise in large language models (LLMs) and retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities. we can deploy a sovereign model like Mistral 7B Instruct, which has strong French-language performance and is self-hostable, to provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk67> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To facilitate access to information and improve answer quality, we can utilize we RAG capabilities, including dense vector retrieval and semantic chunking strategies. we experience with vector stores such as Qdrant and Weaviate will enable we to efficiently manage and retrieve relevant information from existing systems. To reduce processing times, we can optimize the model's performance using quantization methods like INT8 or INT4 (GPTQ), which have been shown to reduce energy consumption while maintaining comparable task performance. we average accuracy gain from fine-tuning is around 12%, which can be achieved through LoRA, QLoRA, or full fine-tuning on domain-specific corpora." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk68> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To integrate with existing systems, we will focus on developing APIs and interfaces that allow seamless interaction between we solution and the municipal agents' work environment. we experience with system integration and technical constraints will ensure a smooth deployment process. Regarding explicability of recommendations, we can employ explainability methods such as source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, or LIME to provide transparent and trustworthy outputs. we EU AI Act limited risk compliance and bias testing process will guarantee that our solution meets regulatory requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk69> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, we are aware of known trade-offs, including the explicability vs. performance trade-off, where sovereign open-weight models like Mistral 7B Instruct may achieve lower relevance scores (~84%) compared to larger proprietary models (~92%). Additionally, online learning from user data is prohibited due to GDPR constraints, and we will rely on offline quarterly fine-tuning on anonymized data instead." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk7> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Interfaces of API type will be expected. 6. Sovereignty constraints the local authority grants a particular importance to the sovereignty of the data. To this title: the hosting will have to be realized on an infrastructure of SecNumCloud type or equivalent, a particular attention will be brought to the dependence vis-à-vis non-European suppliers. 7." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk70> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Overall, our solution combines the strengths of LLMs, RAG, and explainability methods to provide intelligent assistance to municipal agents while addressing technical, regulatory, and environmental constraints." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message14> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk71> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "The City of Belval aims to reduce the environmental footprint of The City of Belval systems of information. The proposed solution should contribute to reducing energetic consumption and rely on infrastructures with low carbon impact." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk72> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "What sustainability measures can we implement to meet these requirements, and what are the known sustainability trade-offs? To reduce the environmental footprint of its systems of informationus Engineering S.r.l. can implement several sustainability measures. our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have a green hosting partnership with OVHcloud and Scaleway, both located in France, which use 100% renewable energy and have low power usage effectiveness (PUE) ratings of 1.3 and 1.28 respectively.  our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. also practice digital sobriety through techniques such as INT8/INT4 model quantisation, which reduces GPU energy consumption by approximately 40%, auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy with a minimum 5-year lifecycle." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk73> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Additionally, our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have an e-waste management partnership with Ecologic in France, ensuring responsible recycling of electronic waste. our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. carbon reporting capability is based on the GRI Standards (partial), allowing our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. to track and reduce our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. carbon footprint. On average, our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. solutions achieve a 35% reduction in energy consumption compared to baseline scenarios." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk74> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are aware of potential sustainability trade-offs. For instance, high availability requirements may conflict with energy reduction goals, as seen in our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. known CSR tension regarding \"high_availability_vs_energy\". conflict is typically resolved by implementing low-power standby modes that can quickly wake up when needed, which our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have found to be compatible with 99.9% uptime SLAs." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk75> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Another trade-off involves the choice between on-premise servers and green energy, as described in our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. \"on_premise_vs_green_energy\" CSR tension." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk76> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "In such cases, our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. recommend that clients subscribe to renewable energy Guarantee of Origin certificates to ensure clients electricity comes from sustainable sources. Lastly, the performance of larger models versus smaller, more energy-efficient ones is a consideration, as outlined in our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk77> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "\"performance_vs_model_size\" CSR tension. our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. typically prefer quantised mid-size models with fine-tuning over large unoptimised models to balance performance and environmental impact. By implementing these sustainability measures and being mindful of potential trade-offs, our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. believe our company Nexus Engineering S.r.l. can help The City of Belval achieve The City of Belval goal of reducing the environmental footprint of The City of Belval systems of information while maintaining high performance standards." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message16> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk78> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "# 1. Executive Summary Nexus Engineering S.r.l., in consortium with specialized partners, proposes an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in municipal agents of the City of Belval daily administrative tasks. an artificial intelligence solution to assist municipal agents of the City of Belval in their daily administrative tasks leverages large language models (LLMs), retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) capabilities, and explainability methods to provide intelligent assistance while addressing technical, regulatory, and environmental constraints. # 2." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk79> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Understanding of Requirements the City of Belval seeks an AI-powered solution that facilitates access to information, improves answer quality, reduces processing times, and integrates with existing systems while ensuring high availability, security, and compliance with GDPR regulations. The project has a total budget of €3 million over four years and aims for minimal environmental impact. # 3." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk8> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Budgetary constraints The global budget allocated to the project is estimated at 3 million euros over a duration of 4 years. The annual cost of exploitation will have to remain mastered and compatible with the budgetary capacities of the local authority. The holder will have to propose an approach allowing to optimize the costs while guaranteeing the quality of service expected. 8." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk80> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Proposed Solution Proposed Solution utilizes the Mistral 7B Instruct model, a sovereign French-language LLM that can be self-hosted to ensure data sovereignty. For RAG capabilities, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will employ dense vector retrieval using Qdrant or Weaviate as Nexus Engineering S.r.l. vector store, enabling efficient management and retrieval of relevant information from existing systems." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk81> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To meet the response time requirement of less than 2 seconds, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will leverage Cloud architecture expertise using Docker and Kubernetes (K8s) for containerization and scalability. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. experience with monitoring tools like Prometheus, Grafana, and ELK stack ensures optimal system performance." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk82> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "For integration, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will use API standards such as REST, GraphQL, or SOAP to integrate with business software (civil status, town planning), electronic management of documents (EDM) systems like Alfresco or OpenKM, and user directories. Nexus Engineering S.r.l. have experience hosting on SecNumCloud-certified infrastructure within the EU, specifically with Outscale and OVHcloud." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk83> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To ensure explicability and transparency, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. will implement explainability methods such as source citation (RAG grounding), chain-of-thought display, SHAP for classification models, or LIME. Proposed Solution complies with GDPR regulations through ISO 27001 certification, anonymization tools like Microsoft Presidio, and a Data Protection Officer (DPO) appointed." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk84> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. budget is aligned with The project total value of €3 million over four years. While Nexus Engineering S.r.l. cannot provide a specific projected margin without additional information, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. target gross margin percentage is 28%, and Nexus Engineering S.r.l. minimum acceptable margin percentage is 18%." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk85> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "To reduce environmental impact, Nexus Engineering S.r.l. partner with green hosting providers OVHcloud and Scaleway, utilizing 100% renewable energy and implementing digital sobriety techniques such as model quantization (INT8/INT4), auto-scaling to zero outside business hours, query result caching, and a green IT hardware procurement policy. # 4. Unaddressed Requirements No specific requirements mentioned in the tender are left unaddressed by Nexus Engineering S.r.l. proposal, given the information provided by the agents." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk86> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "However, ongoing monitoring of updates to the AI Act and other relevant regulations is necessary to ensure compliance throughout The project duration. # 5. Conclusion Nexus Engineering S.r.l., along with Nexus Engineering S.r.l. consortium partners, offers a comprehensive solution that addresses the City of Belval needs for an artificial intelligence-powered assistance tool. our proposal integrates technical expertise in AI/ML, security and compliance measures, cost-effective solutions, and sustainability practices to provide a robust and environmentally conscious system." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk87> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Nexus Engineering S.r.l. are confident that Nexus Engineering S.r.l. approach will enhance the efficiency of municipal services while respecting all regulatory and environmental requirements." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message17> .

    <http://example.org/node/chunk9> a prov:Entity ;
        ex:hasText "Environmental constraints In the framework of City of Belval policy of sustainable development, City of Belval wishes to limit the environmental footprint of City of Belval systems of information. The holder will have to propose a solution contributing to the reduction of the energetic consumption and relying, as much as possible, on infrastructures with low carbon impact. 9. Modalities of deployment the project will have to be conducted in a progressive manner, with: a pilot phase on a limited scope, a progressive generalization to the entirety of the services." ;
        prov:wasDerivedFrom <http://example.org/node/message0> .

